# Demon Slayer Corps – Habit Tracker  
### “Focus, Fight, Forge”

> A mobile‑first, gamified habit‑tracking experience that turns daily routines into a **RPG‑style loop** – complete habits, slay demons, repair your sword, and earn story‑driven rewards.  

---  

## 1️⃣ Overview  

| Aspect | Description |
|---|---|
| **Target Platforms** | Capacitor JS → native iOS / Android + Web (PWA fallback) |
| **Core Gameplay Loop** | 1️⃣ **Select a Demon** (focus timer) → 2️⃣ **Complete timer** (Pomodoro) → 3️⃣ **Earn XP & sword durability** → 4️⃣ **Crow reacts** (narration) |
| **Primary Motivation** | Loss‑aversion (sword durability degrades) + **instant feedback** (crow’s voice, UI glow) |
| **Security** | Biometric + Privacy‑screen overlay, Row‑Level Security (RLS) on every user table, JWT‑based Supabase auth |
| **Design System** | Dark‑theme, glass‑morphism cards, custom color palette (HSL‑tuned), Tailwind 4 + CSS variables, micro‑animations (`shake`, `demon‑pulse`) |
| **State Management** | `zustand` store (`habitStore`, `securityStore`) with **selective persistence** (`localStorage`) for UI state only; all game data lives in Supabase. |

---  

## 2️⃣ Architecture  

```
┌───────────────────────┐
│   React (Vite) UI      │
│  - src/components/*   │
│  - src/stores/*       │
│  - index.css (Tailwind)│
└───────▲───────▲───────┘
        │       │
        │       │
   Capacitor (native)   ←  (Bridge for Biometric, Push)
        │
        ▼
┌───────────────────────┐
│   Supabase Backend    │
│  - Auth (JWT)         │
│  - Postgres DB         │
│  - RLS Policies        │
│  - Edge Functions?    │
└───────────────────────┘
```

### 2.1 Data Flow  

1. **Login** → Supabase JWT stored in `localStorage` (via `authStore`).  
2. **App loads** → `habitStore` fetches user profile, techniques, logs.  
3. **User starts a Demon Encounter** → UI component starts local timer (JS `setInterval`).  
4. **Timer finishes** → `finishEncounter()` writes a row into `encounter_logs` (via Supabase client).  
5. **Server‑side trigger** (none needed – we calculate XP client‑side) → UI updates profile (`xp`, `sword_durability`).  
6. **Crow component** reads updated profile and emits a narration line (audio 🎧 optional).  

---  

## 3️⃣ Database Schema (PostgreSQL)  

### 3.1 Tables  

| Table | Purpose | Key Columns |
|---|---|---|
| `profiles` | User profile, avatar, sword state | `id (PK)`, `display_name`, `total_xp`, `sword_durability`, `crow_status` |
| `breathing_techniques` | Habit definitions (techniques) | `id (PK)`, `user_id (FK)`, `name`, `stamina_cost` |
| `slayer_logs` | Habit completion history | `id (PK)`, `technique_id (FK)`, `user_id (FK)`, `executed_at`, `xp_gained` |
| `encounter_logs` | Focus‑timer sessions | `id (PK)`, `user_id (FK)`, `duration_minutes`, `xp_gained`, `completed_at` |

### 3.2 Indexes  

```sql
CREATE INDEX idx_techniques_user ON public.breathing_techniques(user_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_logs_user ON public.slayer_logs(user_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_logs_date ON public.slayer_logs(executed_at);
CREATE INDEX idx_logs_technique ON public.slayer_logs(technique_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_encounter_user ON public.encounter_logs(user_id);
```

### 3.3 Row‑Level Security (RLS)  

```sql
-- Enable RLS
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.breathing_techniques ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.slayer_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.encounter_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Profiles: only own row
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own profile" ON public.profiles
  FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = id);
CREATE POLICY "Users can update own profile" ON public.profiles
  FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid() = id);
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own profile" ON public.profiles
  FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = id);

-- Techniques: full CRUD on own techniques
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own techniques" ON public.breathing_techniques
  FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = user_id);
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own techniques" ON public.breathing_techniques
  FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);
CREATE POLICY "Users can update own techniques" ON public.breathing_techniques
  FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid() = user_id);
CREATE POLICY "Users can delete own techniques" ON public.breathing_techniques
  FOR DELETE USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Slayer logs: only own logs
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own logs" ON public.slayer_logs
  FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = user_id);
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own logs" ON public.slayer_logs
  FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);
CREATE POLICY "Users can delete own logs" ON public.slayer_logs
  FOR DELETE USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Encounter logs: only own sessions
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own encounters" ON public.encounter_logs
  FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = user_id);
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own encounters" ON public.encounter_logs
  FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);
CREATE POLICY "Users can delete own encounters" ON public.encounter_logs
  FOR DELETE USING (auth.uid() = user_id);
```

*All policies ensure **zero data leakage** between users.*  

